---
description: Layering, state and structure rules for Dart code
globs: lib/**/*.dart
alwaysApply: false
---

- Dependency direction: `ui -> providers/controllers -> repositories -> data`. A feature never imports another feature's `ui/`.
- Widgets only render `AsyncValue`s and call controller or repository methods. No business rules, no Drift queries, no `DateTime.now()` (use `nowProvider`).
- State is Riverpod (ADR-0001): `StreamProvider` for database reads, `Notifier` for UI-only state shared across widgets or surviving navigation, plain classes for repositories. Never `ref.read` inside `build`. Repository providers are not auto-disposed.
- Local ephemeral UI state (field values, submitting flag, inline form errors, segmented selection) is `StatefulWidget` state — typically via `FormSheetScaffold` (ADR-0007). Sync blank-title validation may stay in the widget. `TextEditingController`, `FocusNode`, and `ScrollController` are pure Flutter plumbing and stay in the widget's State class.
- Undo callbacks run from SnackBars that outlive screens: capture the repository before navigating; show Undo through `AppMessenger`.
- Do not add a domain layer, repository interfaces, freezed, json_serializable or any other state library (ADR-0003).
- Prefer `const`, small widgets and narrow `ref.watch` scopes. Split files before they pass about 300 lines.
- Folder layout follows `docs/architecture.md` section 2.3.
- UI write, failure and form conventions: follow ADR-0007.
